# .dockerignore keeps the build context Dockerfile's stage-1 `make dist`
# runs against small, without excluding anything that target needs (its
# own `web-build` + `lint-web-assets` + `go build -tags web_assets`
# recipe touches nearly every tracked directory in this repository,
# including test/ and contracts/ -- narvichecks's own `./...` scope and
# pushpr.go's own contracts/ import respectively -- so this list is
# deliberately narrow: build tooling, dependency caches, and worktrees,
# never source).

# Git metadata -- never needed inside the build context, and often the
# single largest thing in it.
.git
.gitignore

# Sibling git worktrees checked out alongside this one (this repository's
# own multi-worktree development convention, CLAUDE.md) -- never inside
# this checkout's own directory tree in practice, listed defensively in
# case a worktree is ever created as a subdirectory.
.worktrees/
worktrees/

# npm dependencies -- COPY web/package.json web/package-lock.json + npm ci
# inside the build stage installs these fresh; a host checkout's own
# node_modules/ (if `npm install` was ever run locally) must never be
# copied in over that fresh install.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
contracts/node_modules/

# Go/npm build artifacts a local checkout may have lying around (.gitignore's
# own list) -- never something `make dist` reads, always something it
# writes.
/narvi
/control-plane
/sandbox-agent
/contractspatch
/narvichecks
/internal/adapters/inbound/webui/dist

# Test/coverage artifacts and editor/OS cruft -- never inputs to the
# build.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
.DS_Store
.env
.vscode/
.idea/
